# Signify when a resource is OFF in the planning views

## Chosen design (from your answers)

- OFF is a **partial percentage per week** (e.g. 40% off), independent of any project.
- **No reason/label** — just `offPct`.
- Editing happens **directly in the by-resource grid** via a dedicated "OFF" row; the by-project view shows it read-only.

## Why this fits the codebase

The whole app is already weekly: `Booking` is keyed by `(resourceId, projectId, weekStart)` in [prisma/schema.prisma](prisma/schema.prisma). OFF is the same shape minus the project, so it maps cleanly to a new sibling table and a new grid row type. It stays "linked to a resource, not a project" by construction, and add/update/delete reuse the exact inline-cell pattern already used for allocations.

## Data model — new table

Add to [prisma/schema.prisma](prisma/schema.prisma):

```prisma
model ResourceTimeOff {
  id         String   @id @default(uuid())
  resourceId String
  weekStart  DateTime
  offPct     Int      // 1..100, percent of the week the resource is unavailable
  resource   Resource @relation(fields: [resourceId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  createdAt  DateTime @default(now())
  updatedAt  DateTime @updatedAt

  @@unique([resourceId, weekStart])
  @@index([weekStart])
  @@index([resourceId, weekStart])
}
```

Add `timeOff ResourceTimeOff[]` to the `Resource` model. Then run a Prisma migration (`prisma migrate dev`) — this is the only DB change.

## Server actions + validation

- [src/lib/validations.ts](src/lib/validations.ts): add `timeOffSchema` (`resourceId`, `weekStart`, `offPct` 1..100).
- [src/app/planning/actions.ts](src/app/planning/actions.ts): add `setResourceTimeOff(data)` (upsert on `[resourceId, weekStart]`; `offPct <= 0` deletes the row) and `deleteResourceTimeOff(id)`, each calling `revalidatePath("/planning")`. Mirrors the existing `createBooking`/`deleteBooking` style.

## Data loading

[src/app/planning/page.tsx](src/app/planning/page.tsx): add a 4th query for `db.resourceTimeOff.findMany` over the visible week range (active resources), and pass `timeOff` into `PlanningGrid`.

## View model

[src/lib/planning-view-model.ts](src/lib/planning-view-model.ts):

- Add `TimeOffModel` and a new `PlanningRowType` value `"off"`.
- Build an `offByWeek` map keyed `${resourceId}:${wk}` -> `offPct` (helper like the existing `resourceWeekTotals`).
- In the **by-resource** branch of `buildPlanningMatrix`, push an `"off"` row into each resource group (next to the existing `summary` row).
- Cells carry `offPct` so both views can read it.

## UI

- New component `src/components/planning/EditableOffCell.tsx`: a trimmed copy of [EditableAllocationCell.tsx](src/components/planning/EditableAllocationCell.tsx) — numeric % input, no project, no note; empty/0 deletes. Calls `setResourceTimeOff`/`deleteResourceTimeOff`.
- [src/components/planning/PlanningTableBody.tsx](src/components/planning/PlanningTableBody.tsx):
  - Render the `"off"` row (label "OFF") in by-resource view using `EditableOffCell`.
  - In **by-project** view, when a resource is off in a week, render a read-only marker on that allocation cell (subtle striped/“OFF” background + tooltip like `40% off`).
  - Update the over-allocation logic: available = `100 - offPct`, so `OverloadHint` and the summary `TotalPctPill` flag a week when `bookedTotal > 100 - offPct` (today it uses `> 100`).
- Thread the off data through [PlanningGrid.tsx](src/components/planning/PlanningGrid.tsx) -> `PlanningTable` -> `PlanningTableBody` (same prop-drilling as `resWeekTotals`).

