## Technical impact

- **Scope:** ~8-10 files; one new table + one migration; one new small component.
- **Risk: low.** OFF is an additive, separate table and a separate row type; existing booking create/update/delete/undo paths are untouched. The only shared logic touched is the over-allocation threshold in the by-resource summary.
- **Out of scope / optional follow-ups:** undo-redo support for OFF edits (booking history currently assumes a `projectId`); managing OFF from the resource screen; bulk "off for N weeks".

